{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766656-dragonslaying-and-sacrificial-lamb","id":766656,"title":"Dragonslaying and Sacrificial Lamb","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-15T16:57:29-08:00","id":766656,"title":"Dragonslaying and Sacrificial Lamb","content":"So I was looking through the Hurt Locker draft today (for those who haven't seen: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/into-the-hurt-locker/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/into-the-hurt-locker/</a> ) and I noticed under the &quot;Template&quot; a couple of rather intriguing Merits that don't appear to have made it to the Kickstarter draft, and maybe not to the final cut. These Merits are titled, respectively, Dragonslaying and Sacrificial Lamb, which are probably both Hero-related Merits. Now, if these didn't make it into the Backer/near-final version, maybe they're being saved for the <b>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes </b>supplement.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of wondering if the devs would be so kind as to release the draft versions if neither of those things are true, because they sound really interesting.<br /> <br /> Interesting things the Merits suggest: Followers are a big deal for Heroes, and/or they were originally supposed to have slightly more permanent groups of Followers/Cultists. Or Beasts could have Cultists. Or something along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 11-15-2015, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T17:03:35-08:00","id":766663,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, totally missed those didn't make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T17:35:42-08:00","id":766680,"title":"","content":"Sacrificial Lamb got folded into the Hero template by default, but the mechanics are a bit different. Not sure what became of Dragonslaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%